yuma123-netconfd-module-ietf-hardware-state-matter (1.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Matter over Thread implementation: sensor readings come from the Open Home
    Foundation Matter Server (python-matter-server) through the Python helper
    ietf-hardware-state-matter (standard library only, own WebSocket client)
  * Each Matter node, e.g. IKEA ALPSTUGA, is a container component with
    temperature, humidity, co2, pm25 and air-quality sensor components;
    offline nodes are reported with oper-status unavailable
  * Helper subcommands nodes, commission (Thread dataset from OTBR) and thread-dataset
  * MATTER_NODE_ID selects one node for one netconfd instance per device
  * example/docker-compose.yml for OTBR (ZBT-2) and Matter Server,
    test/mock-matter-server for testing without hardware
  * Removed the STS3x/PMS7003 I2C/UART code

